{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3536","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3536","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3536\",\"parent_revision\":\"1f68264aabf594409ee3593a3dea9bed7df0d94c1872da3f88c7b0d9f01ed3ff\",\"root_revision\":\"1f68264aabf594409ee3593a3dea9bed7df0d94c1872da3f88c7b0d9f01ed3ff\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-review-rubric.md` Gate 2 scores Rule 2a as: \\\"Any such figure anywhere in the entry, including inside a badge, a quoted README passage, or a 'Key Statistics' section that should not exist.\\\"\\n\\nThat section was required by the entry template until commit `a54eef252` (2026-07-08, PR #2723) deleted the `Key Statistics` block \u2014 `GitHub Stars`, `Downloads/month`, `Contributors` \u2014 from `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-template.md`. Verified in that commit's diff. Every entry authored before that date therefore carries the section by construction, because the template it was written against demanded it.\\n\\nConsequence: a `--rerun` refresh of any pre-2026-07-08 entry trips a Rule 2a defect for having obeyed the template in force at the time. A Gate 2 defect drives `REQUEST CHANGES`, which withholds the entry's README row (SKILL.md Post-Actions step 1), so the entry drops out of the index for a rule that did not exist when it was written. The rule reads as a statement about entry content when what it governs is an agent's gathering behaviour.\\n\\nThe repo owner has ruled that existing statistics stay. Any rule about popularity statistics governs an agent gathering them \u2014 the prohibition binds at gather time, applies whether or not the repository is in the session's authorized GitHub scope, and admits no fallback source (web search, package registry, a README badge). It does not bind the existing files. A figure in a finished entry is not a defect, not a `--fix` target, and not a reason to edit or withhold that entry.\\n\\nTwo places state the rule and both need to agree: the fidelity rule in `entry-quality-standards.md` (the writing contract) and the Gate 2 row in `entry-review-rubric.md` (the audit). Today only the audit half asserts retroactivity, so fixing one file alone leaves the contradiction in place.\\n\\nSame false-defect class as #3534 and the creation-target fix already shipped in PR #3532: a gate scoring text that was correct when written.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the original wording is in closed PR #3528, commit `0f3a15bf6`, in the `entry-quality-standards.md` Rule 2a rewrite. It was left out of the salvage PR because it changes whether a finished entry is withheld from the index, which is verdict mechanics rather than salvage. The historical fact and its citation (`a54eef252`, 2026-07-08) are the durable part.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 salvage review of closing PRs #3527 and #3528 (PR #3532)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5aa00133590489b40b3c9a6040552e713de0ee368955e52b769c9487a16100a3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUPu2AQ\"}"}